        "original_id": "aee381c8-e4b8-528c-847d-d3cfbc4771ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Del Davis\n- Groups: Peter and Gordon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Songs: \"A World Without Love\", \"World Without Love\"\n- Albums: \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop duo Peter and Gordon.\n- Peter and Gordon's biggest hit was the No. 1 million-selling song \"A World Without Love\".\n- Paul McCartney wrote \"A World Without Love\" and it was attributed to Lennon–McCartney.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\" that was featured on the album \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
